A||||9||Gold-86SE||San Antonio Boneyard Has Booku Fieros||||1||
Z||000000||Gold-86SE||12-23-2000||10:09 AM||||<BR>Attention South Central Texas Members. The Pick-n-Pull on Highway 16 going toward Poteet has several Fieros.  Several 84s, one or two 85 and 86s (but not exactly sure) and one 88 model, all four cylinders.  Not completely sure of year model count, but I know there are 84s and one 88, in total, there about six Fieros.<P>These have been picked over for some interior stuff and some engine parts, but I noticed some light grey/gray interior(s) and dashes in fairly good condition.  Lots and lots of body panels, the 88 still had it's front and rear bumper facia, white in color.  The 88 could be saved, if the lot would sell it, it just occured to me that I should have grabbed that VIN. Additionally, there are several auto and manual transmissions.<P>Myself, I was able to get an e-brake boot, head light switch and a black remote deck lid release switch from an 84, and horn paddles - man what a find.  I even pulled a notchback (sorry I accidently tore the driver side quarter panel, man that pissed me off.)  Total spent, 62 bucks.<P>I would offer to go back and hunt parts for folks, but I am going to be out-of-town and unable to do such a task.  The trip to Pick-n-Pull was on a fluke anyhow, but I wanted to share the information.  Hope someone benefits, besides just me.<BR><P>------------------<BR>84 SE 4.10 4 Speed (Cold and Rain Daily Driver)<BR>85 GT Automatic (Restoration Project)<BR>86 SE 4 Speed (Fair Weather Daily Driver)<BR>87 SC 5 Speed (Not Running, V8 Conversion?)||||reg||1
Z||000001||mshill||12-23-2000||04:43 PM||||I had a disppointing day at the three Pick-n-Pulls in the Sacramento, CA area. All I got was a short shifter.  I hit all three and there were probably only nine Fieros between the three.  Most of them I had seen before and were very well picked over.<P>Good news though,  New Years day they are having a half price sale.  I was thinking about going and grabbing a 3.1 short block<BR>that I saw.  I have always been too hard pressed to try and remove one from a car (too much time required), but this one just needed  a couple mounting bolts to be removed and it is out.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||HAGS||12-23-2000||04:54 PM||||THANK YOU!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000003||HAGS||12-24-2000||04:58 AM||||I'll probably head out there tomorrow, do you know if it was north or south of 1604??<P>If anyone wants me to look for something I'll try, I only have $200 in my pocket and I still need to shop for my brother, dad, and sister....any left over will probably goto a replacement TBI.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Indiana_resto_guy||12-24-2000||07:32 AM||||Hags,<P>Please check and see what they want for the left front upper and lower control arms off the '88. I'll reimburse you for your effort if the price is right.<BR>Thanks in advance! (Oh, tomorrow is Christmas! Have a good one!)||||reg||1
Z||000005||Gold-86SE||12-24-2000||11:25 AM||||<BR>HAGS, the way I went (because I live near Selma) is IH35 South to Loop 410 West, then took the Highway 16 exit going toward Poteet. <P>Pick-n-Pull is outside the 410 Loop and is approximately one mile from the Loop, if that far.  I don't know the name of the road that I have to make a left on, but it winds behind a jail house and a mobile home park then the Pick-n-Pull is on the right-hand side. Hope that helps.<P>Since I am trying to make this a fast post, I did not look up the address in the phone book, but try the San Antonio yellow pages for the exact address.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Gold-86SE||12-24-2000||11:33 AM||||<BR>Just remembered something, hence the quick post after-the-fact.<P>When you go to Pick-n-Pull, grab that VIN on the 88, there is a guy here on PFF (I forget his screen name) that is wanting the location, condition and VIN of all 88s.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||HAGS||12-25-2000||11:56 PM||||I went out there on Christmas Eve but of course they were closed, forgot my tools anyway, I'll probably go back on saturday, the 30th, if anyone else wants me to look for stuff.||||reg||1
Z||000008||HAGS||12-30-2000||08:05 PM||||I got out there today, thought I was going to be disappointed 5 fieros gutted of all the stuff I need then I come up on another with the decklid closed...I pick the lock and there sits everything I needed, nothing was missing in the engine compartment.  Got myself the TBI, PCV Valve, Engine cradle bolt, air filter cover.<P>The control arms on the 88 Fiero were $15 each I believe, they have a general price for all control arms, they didnt look too hot but I guess they could be cleaned up.  The 88 was pretty gutted but I pulled the VIN<BR>1G2PE11R7JP224964||||reg||1
Z||000009||Cheever2||12-30-2000||09:02 PM||||I guess it's too late to ask for a shifter?<BR>Maybe next time, huh?  I'm in no hurry anyway.<BR><P>------------------<BR><I>Chuck Hodges</I>||||reg||6
